### Why `tileSize: 256` matters
* The raster source defaults to `tileSize: 512`.  
* OSM’s tiles are 256 px, so without overriding the size the imagery will appear at the wrong zoom level (labels and other vector layers will be mis-aligned, and the map can look “off-scale”).

### Optional but useful additions
| Property | Why you might want it |
|----------|----------------------|
| `minzoom` / `maxzoom` | Constrains requests to the zoom range the server actually provides (OSM: 0-19). |
| `attribution` | Required by OSM’s license and shows up in the map’s UI if you use a control that displays it. |
| `bounds` (if you want to limit the view) | Not required for OSM, but useful for custom tile sets. |

### CORS
OpenStreetMap tiles already send the proper `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` header, so no extra CORS configuration is needed.

With the `tileSize: 256` (and the source-layer added to a raster layer) the OSM raster tiles will render correctly in MapLibre.
